{"id":"word:hebrew:H6996","type":"word","title":"קָטָן","subtitle":"H6996 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"abbreviated , i.e. diminutive , literally (in quantity, size or number) or figuratively (in age or importance)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to קָטָן (H6996) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: a.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 101 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"קָטָן (qâṭân) means abbreviated , i.e. diminutive , literally (in quantity, size or number) or figuratively (in age or importance) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 12 15."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"קָטָן","transliteration":"qâṭân","pronunciation":"kaw-tawn'","strong":"H6996","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6996","partOfSpeech":"a","forms":["קָטֹ֖ן","הַ/קָּטֹ֖ן","הַ/קָּטֹן֙","הַ/קָּטָ֔ן","הַ/קָּטָֽן"],"morphs":[["HTd/Aamsa",29],["HAamsa",24],["HAafsa",9],["HR/Aamsa",7],["HTd/Aafsa",6],["HRd/Aamsa",4],["HTd/Aampa",3],["HAampa",2],["HR/R/Aamsa",2],["HC/Aafsa",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"abbreviated , i.e. diminutive , literally (in quantity, size or number) or figuratively (in age or importance)","usage":"least, less(-er), little (one), small(-est, one, quantity, thing), young(-er, -est).","full":"H6996. qatan I. קָטָן adjective small, young, unimportant ; — absolute ׳ק Gen 9:24 +; suffix קְטַנָּם (Kö ii.l,74 ) Jer 6:13 +; feminine singular קְטַנָּה Gen 29:16 +; masculine plural קְטַנִּים 2Kin 18:24 +; construct קְטַנֵּי 1Sam 9:21 (see Dr; We conjectures נִּי -, old construct, cf, HPS), Prov 30:24 ; feminine plural קְטַנּוֺת Ezek 16:61 +; — 1 small ; especially a. of children, youth = young , Gen 44:20 (J) 2Sam 9:12 ; 1Kin 11:17 ; 2Kin 2:23 ; 5:2 , of sister Song 8:8 ; = younger , of two children (often opposed to גדול ), Gen 9:24 ; 27:15 , 42 (all J), 29:16 , 18 (E), 1Sam 14:49 (feminine; opposed to הַבְּכִירָה ); of younger sister Judg 15:2 , so (figurative) Ezek 16:46 and (+ מִן compare) 16:61 ; brother 1Chr 24:31 ; ׳הַקּ youngest son (of several) 1Sam 16:11 ; 17:14 ; גָּדוֺל = young and old (see קָטֹן 1 ) Jer 16:6 compare 2Chr 31:15 ; 34:30 . b. of things : utterance Num 22:18 (E), weight Deut 25:13-14 , vessels 2Chr 36:18 , animals Psa 104:25 (all opposed to גדול ); compare also 2Sam 12:3 ; 1Kin 2:20 ; 17:13 ; 18:44 ; 2Kin 4:10 ; Ezek 43:14 (opposed to גדול ), Prov 30:24 ; Song 2:15 , + probably Ezek 46:22 (see II. [ קָטַר ]); הַקָּטָן כְּלֵי Isa 22:24 the vessels of small size (figurative). 2 small ; a. with added idea of weakness, person 2Kin 18:24 = Isa 36:9 , city Eccl 9:14 . b. = insignificant , (I) tribe 1Sam 9:21 ; (2) person (+ גדול ; = all persons) Jer 6:13 ; 31:34 ; Jonah 3:5 ; Psa 115:13 ; Est 1:5 , 20 , cf . 1Chr 12:14 (van d. H. v. 12:13 ); (3) in General, קְטַנּוֺת יוֺם Zech 4:10 day of small things. — See also קָטֹן . קָטֹן 54 adjective small, insignificant ; — absolute ׳ק 1Sam 2:19 +; construct קְטֹן 2Chr 21:17 ; — f., plural and suffix supplied by קָטָן ; — 1 small: especially a. of youth = young , קּ ׳נַעַר 1Sam 20:35 ; 1Kin 3:7 ; 2Kin 5:14 ; Isa 11:6 ; = younger of two brothers, Gen 48:19 (E) Judg 1:13 ; 3:9 (+ מִן compare); ׳הַקּ youngest brother Gen 42:13 10 t. Genesis (JE), son Judg 9:5 ; 2Chr 22:1 , so בָּנָיו קְטֹן 21:17 ; + גדול = young and old (see קָטָן 1 ), i.e. everybodty Gen 19:11 (J), 1Sam 5:9 ; 30:2 +? 30:19 . b. of things 1Sam 2:19 ; 1Kin 8:64 (+ מִן compare), Amos 6:11 ; Isa 54:7 ; opposed to גָּדוֺל 1Sam 22:15 ; 25:36 ; Gen 1:16 (P). 2 = unimportant , things, Exod 18:22 , 26 (E), 1Sam 20:2 (all opposed to גדול ); person,= feeble Amos 7:2 , 5 ; = insignificant Jer 49:15 ; Obadiah 2 (both || בָּזוּי ), Isa 60:22 (|| צָעִיר ); ׳ק בְּעֵינֶיךָ 1Sam 15:17 ; especially + גָּדוֺל = low and high, + everybody, Deut 1:17 ; 1Kin 22:31 2Chr 18:30 ; Jer 8:10 ; Job 3:19 , +8 t. — See also קָטָן .","rootNote":"or קָטֹן ; from 6962 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"first